n_id":"tvfy_10387","person_slug":"sussan-ley","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tanya Plibersek","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10513","person_slug":"tanya-plibersek","vote":"no"},{"name":"Ted O'Brien","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10866","person_slug":"ted-obrien","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Terri Butler","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10825","person_slug":"terri-butler","vote":"no"},{"name":"Terry Young","party":"LNP","person_id":"tvfy_10933","person_slug":"terry-young","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tim Watts","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10794","person_slug":"tim-watts","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tim Wilson","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10894","person_slug":"tim-wilson","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tony Burke","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10081","person_slug":"tony-burke","vote":"no"},{"name":"Tony Pasin","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10784","person_slug":"tony-pasin","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Tony Zappia","party":"Labor","person_id":"tvfy_10695","person_slug":"tony-zappia","vote":"no"},{"name":"Trent Zimmerman","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10844","person_slug":"trent-zimmerman","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Vince Connelly","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10939","person_slug":"vince-connelly","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Warren Entsch","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10203","person_slug":"warren-entsch","vote":"aye"},{"name":"Zali Steggall","party":"Independent","person_id":"tvfy_10941","person_slug":"zali-steggall","vote":"aye"}],"name":"Australia's Foreign Relations (State and Territory Arrangements) Bill 2020 - Second Reading - Redraft bill","noes":44,"question":"The majority voted in favour of keeping the wording of the usual second reading motion unchanged. The usual [second reading motion](https://peo.gov.au/understand-our-parliament/how-parliament-works/bills-and-laws/making-a-law-in-the-australian-parliament/) is \"*That the bill be read for a second time*,\" which is parliamentary jargon for agreeing with the main idea of the bill. The MP for Corio [Richard Marles](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/representatives/corio/richard_marles) (Labor) had proposed to delete the words after 'that' and replace them with the words below. ### Motion text > *That all words after \"That\" be omitted with a view to substituting the following words:* > > *\"whilst not declining to give the bill a second reading, the House:* > > *(1) notes:* > >> *(a) the desirability of greater oversight and review mechanisms for decisions made under the bill; and* >> >> *(b) the lack of clarity in the definition of 'arrangements' and 'institutional autonomy' in the bill; and* > > *(2) calls on the Government to:* > >> *(a) address the regulatory gap of private universities;* >> >> *(b) provide clarity on the treatment of the Port of Darwin in the bill before the bill proceeds;* >> >> *(c) make clear how this regime will interact with the existing legislation and guidelines that work to safeguard Australia's sovereignty, and provide confidence that the bill does not present a sovereign risk that will undermine investment and cost Australian jobs; engage in genuine consultation with Australian entities covered by the bill on the design of the regime; and* >> >> *(d) redraft the bill and re-present it to the Parliament at the earliest opportunity\"*","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-representatives-6705","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/representatives/2020-11-11/2"}
